{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793311414,"nonce":"Z4yShqn16zrYellhvZXTNARjmvY=","title":"AOT currently shares the JIT's ASH_PROMOTE_MODULE_CAP budget in promote_function_strict. The default cap is 256 bodies. Even though AOT must eventually compile every function, each promotion counts every body in the growing LLVM module, caps pending compilation, and replaces pending definitions with private $via_table trampolines. Later AOT iterations create the real bodies, leaving unnecessary table indirections behind.","message":"Reproducer: /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/RayDE/site/demo, current build.hxml (published Ashui/components/icons 0.2.2, -dce full), rebuilt with RayDE's WASM define and preview filesystem adapter. Measure with -O3 --codegen-opt-level 0 --target wasm32-wasip1-threads, fibers enabled and six shards, matching RayDE's preview defaults. Linux Intel i5-1250P NUC, LLVM 21.1.8, the matched ThinLTO/16-CU host build from 7e105d9e.\n\nBaseline warm build: 19.978 s total, LLVM IR phase 13.999 s, backend 4.852 s, linker 0.938 s. All 2,699 optimized AIR bodies hit; zero lowering/passes. One function-body edit reuses 2,697 optimized bodies but still takes 19.876 s.\n\nASH_PROFILE=phases separates 13.982 s in llvm promote, 13.079 s self, versus only 0.903 s in AIR v2 -\u003e LLVM. It records 2,747 table trampolines and 7,160 total LLVM bodies. ASH_PROMOTE_MODULE_CAP=off drops IR to 0.946 s and total build to 6.684 s, with 4,413 bodies and no table-trampoline counter. This is a separate issue from persistent LLVM artifact reuse: most of the apparent LLVM-IR cost is JIT policy overhead.\n\nFix: AOT must bypass the JIT budget; retain the existing JIT cap. Validate native and WASM virtual calls, closures, getters, catches, and low/default/off cap independence. Check unchanged and edited real demo modules in Chrome with the preview filesystem channel, compare repeated NUC stage times and cold/warm/edit cache behavior, and record the commit/report trail. Related: 8b12bc8, 3b7fa54, c78c3b3, 1cf21d8.","files":null}]}